    </div><div class=3D"para" id=3D"para-45" data-idx=3D"45">
      <span class=3D"para-idx">45</span>
      <h4>Cancer fatalism</h4>
<p>Cancer fatalism was measured at baseline, postintervention, and postatta=
ck using a 20-item scale adapted from Shen et al. (2009) for the cancer con=
text. Rated on 7-point agreement scales, the items captured three dimension=
s of cancer fatalism: predetermination (e.g., "If someone is meant to get c=
ancer, they will get it no matter what they do"), luck (e.g., "Whether I wi=
ll get cancer is a matter of luck"), and pessimism (e.g., "There is really =
no way I can prevent cancer"). Reliabilities across the three assessments w=
