    </div><div class=3D"para" id=3D"para-48" data-idx=3D"48">
      <span class=3D"para-idx">48</span>
      <h4>Intentions to adopt cancer risk-reduction behaviors</h4>
<p>After Phase 1 and Phase 2 message exposure, intentions were assessed for=
 four modifiable behaviors most commonly identified in health guidance as r=
elevant to cancer risk reduction: fruit and vegetable consumption, physical=
 activity, smoking avoidance, and alcohol avoidance. Each was measured with=
 a single item asking how likely participants were to engage in the behavio=
r over the next two weeks (1 =3D extremely unlikely, 7 =3D extremely likely=
).</p>

    </div><div class=3D"para" id=3D"para-49" data-idx=3D"49">
      <span class=3D"para-idx">49</span>
      <h4>Identification and transportation</h4>
<p>Identification and transportation were captured after Phase 1 message ex=
posure with scales adopted from Watts et al. (2025), whose wording suited b=
oth narrative and non-narrative messages. Identification was assessed with =
six items (e.g., "While reading, I felt I could really get inside the autho=
r's head";  <mjx-container class=3D"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0" jax=3D"CHT=
ML" tabindex=3D"0" ctxtmenu_counter=3D"9" style=3D"font-size: 119.2%; posit=
ion: relative;"><mjx-math class=3D"MJX-TEX" aria-hidden=3D"true"><mjx-mi cl=
